director had worked abroad predicted their entire fashion line creativity, but not the number of countries that they worked abroad. That didn't have near as much of an impact as the amount of time that they worked abroad. All these examples have a common thread. The fashion designers look a lot like the students at Business School who dated someone from another country. The students look a lot like the scientists who spend time collaborating with partners from different ethnicities. The musicians who work with someone from a different tradition have something in common with the entrepreneurs who make broad connections and spend time maintaining them. What all these cross cultural relationships have is depth.
总监在海外工作的时间能够预测其整个时装系列的创造力，但他们在多少个国家工作过却不能。后者对创造力的影响远远不及他们在海外工作的时间长短。所有这些例子都有一个共同的线索。时装设计师看起来很像商学院里与另一个国家的人约会过的学生。这些学生看起来很像那些花时间与不同种族背景的伙伴合作的科学家。那些与来自不同传统的人合作的音乐家，与那些建立广泛联系并花时间维护这些联系的企业家有着共同之处。所有这些跨文化关系都具备的共同点是：深度。

